s show on the last page:  [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:165:- Menu: `const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', { label: 'LOAD', disabled: true }], { x: 'center', y: 100, title, onPick(i, item), onCancel, scale: 2, rows: 6 })` (rows: it scrolls); `menu.update(dt) [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:171:- Music: `music('title' | 'adventure' | 'dungeon' | 'boss' | 'victory')` (built in; any other name warns and plays nothing), or your own `{ bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .15, not [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:198:**Attack** (melee timing for swords, punches, kicks): `const slash = new E.Attack('slash')` (a move from `E.MOVES`, optionally with overrides: `new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 })`) or a spec `{ a0, [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:205:**Humanoid** (knights, heroes, soldiers, zombies): `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'chibi' (default) | 'heroic' (tall) | 'bulky' (brawlers, bosses) | 'skeleton' (tint with colors.bone), weapon: 's [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:214:- In steep ground views (threequarter) rigs and Blobs are drawn from a lower, sprite-like angle so faces show, like SNES RPG sprites (`charView: false` turns it off for one rig, `E.style.charPitch = f [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:218:**Blob** (slimes, rabbites, bats, imps, round monsters): `new E.Blob({ R: 6, colors: { dk, base, lt, spec, eye, pupil }, ears: 'rabbit' | 'cat', horns: true, wings: true, feet: true, tail: true, mouth [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:229:| Platformer (Mario, Mega Man, Sonic, Castlevania) | `side` (+ `brawler` for 2.5D) | PlatformMap, Platformer, Humanoid, sprites, Bullets `'side'` | PLATFORMER |\nvendor/engine/API.md:231:| Action adventure (Zelda, Secret of Mana) | `threequarter` or `topdown` | TileMap rows, `cam.room`, Body, Humanoid + `E.Attack` sword, Dialog, `E.ui.hearts` | ADVENTURE |\nvendor/engine/API.md:235:| Beat-'em-up (Final Fight, Streets of Rage, TMNT) | `brawler` | TileMap street strip, Body, Humanoid (`weapon: null`) + `E.Combo` punches and `kick: true` kicks, `E.knockback`, waves that lock the sc [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:246:| Real-time strategy (Warcraft II, StarCraft, Dune II) | `iso` | `E.Strategy` (the strategy module): kinds as data, selection by click, box and group, orders, gold, building, training, fog, an AI's bu [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:248:| 3D platformer or adventure remake (Mario 64, Ocarina, Crash) | `iso` / `threequarter` / `brawler` | TileMap blocks of different heights + Body `jump()` (z is real height); in real 3D: `E.World3D` (t [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:267:The repo (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge; any file at `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/<path>`) holds more to take from. Its files are large: search them and take  [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:268:- **Motion clips**: 325 curated and 2,548 motion-capture takes that play on any Humanoid: find one in `src/mocap/catalogs/`, cut a small set with `tools/anim-set.mjs`, then `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` (`A [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:270:- **Worked examples**: Emberdeep (`src/emberdeep/`), a whole game on this engine: 29 monster, boss and dummy bodies, 3 heroes and 30 skills, registered with `def(kind, id, spec)` (one search lists the [... omitted end of long line]\nvendor/engine/API.md:292:- Title screen and game-over screen as scenes; `pausable: true` on gameplay scenes. No pause, settings, rebinding or full-screen code of your own (they're standard); prompts from `game.input.label(act [... omitted end of long line]\n7:<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Test a game against the AI Hub Session Protocol: 1–4 copies next to each other on a simulated network.\">\n65:<script type=\"module\">\n66:import { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\n67:import { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\n73:const scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\n74:/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\n75:const serverMode = scenario === 'server';\n113: * For a game tagged parallel or ghost, the seed rides in the address: the client seeds Math.random with it before the game's scripts run.\n114: * Only a page of this site is loaded: ?game= comes from the address bar, and a javascript: or another site's\n379: * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\n411:  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\n477:    if (scenario === 'host-leave') removeCell(state.cells[0]);\n505:    if (scenario === 'host-leave' && !SELF_REPORTED.includes(state.coordinator.mode)) {\n527:    document.body.dataset.complete = 'true';\n546:</script>\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
