{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_120","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('tools/browser-test.py');s=p.read_text().replace('def log_message(self, *args):','def log_message(self, format: str, *args: object) -> None:');p.write_text(s)\nPY\nruff check tools/browser-test.py && ruff format tools/browser-test.py && ty check tools/browser-test.py --python /home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\np=pathlib.Path('src/report.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text())\nr['sourceInformation']['tech']='my-3D2dge / World3D v0.89.1 (8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691); three.js 0.182.0; Rapier SIMD compat 0.19.3; AI Hub client 1.4.0 (35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869); browser JavaScript; Bun 1.3.14 bundler.'\nr['sourceInformation']['research']='Read all 17 scanned Mattel manual pages; cross-checked official transcript and publisher history. Retrieved recording excerpt 00:40–01:20 and inspected frames at 00:43, 00:58 and 01:12. Exact original music and timbres unknown; no human listening available. Research links are in docs/RESEARCH.md.'\nr['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless normal-rules solo and co-op routes; exact-HTML keyboard, mouse, emulated standard gamepad and phone/tablet touch tests; WebGPU, WebGL 2, WebKit and unsupported-Firefox handling; Web Audio analysis; real two-context WebRTC; official Hub harness plus server, timeout and departure cases. Physical devices, human listening and cross-network NAT unavailable.'\nr['testingFeedback']=[\n '19 actual implementation issues were caught and fixed; the issue ledger separates them from test-harness mistakes.',\n '0 critical or game-breaking issues were found. Input, menu, co-op access and compatibility defects were fixed before release.',\n 'The complete normal-rules replay against the delivered HTML, including 372 acknowledged inputs over real WebRTC with both peers compared after every action.',\n 'The initial text search for external script tags matched examples inside embedded engine documentation. Actual HTML parsing and browser request checks were more useful.'\n]\nr['engineFeedback']=[\n 'World3D uses the same procedural materials, native shapes and articulated rigs throughout a first-person dungeon; the fixed-step lifecycle and menu/rebinding infrastructure provide useful foundations.',\n 'Native Shell pause bookkeeping needed explicit integration with a live online world. The three.js WebGPU import also expected GPUShaderStage constants on Firefox before renderer capability checks could run.',\n 'The authoritative deterministic two-strength model, six-slot inventory transactions, authored campaign and cooperative round/transport rules.',\n 'Keeping native animation, the first-person camera and menu focus separate from authoritative rules and the independently running network clock.',\n 'none; engine and World3D source files remain unmodified. The HTML supplies the standard GPUShaderStage constants when missing, and the game registers native art, poses, moves and instruments.',\n 'Ship a self-contained first-person crawler example with renderer-free authority, unsupported-renderer handling and documented live-menu behavior.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nnpm run build\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
