{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_167","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> src/ui/style.css <<'EOF'\n.touch-mode .place{max-width:75%}.touch-mode #touch-hint{display:none}\nEOF\ncat >> docs/ISSUES.md <<'EOF'\n\nThe long-menu focus fix in issue18 also rechecks focus after inserted developer/workshop content. The touch-HUD cleanup in issue28 now puts gesture instructions in the dismissible opening card and removes the overlapping persistent hint.\n\n31. Planning-window tuning could not affect a playable co-op setup, while standalone online developer controls appeared editable: noncritical configuration-access defect; validated host invitations now disclose/negotiate2–30-second planning (8 stock), custom durations mark the expedition modified, and all online developer panels are read-only.\n32. Meaningful mouse motion did not exit attract mode: noncritical input consistency defect; moving the mouse now exits and consumes the demo without starting a run.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('src/report.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text());r['testingFeedback'][0]='32 actual implementation issues were caught and fixed; the issue ledger separates them from test-harness mistakes.';r['sourceInformation']['online']='1–2 shared-world co-op: reliable ordered WebRTC DataChannel with manual offer/answer and disclosed 2–30-second planning (8 seconds stock); AI Hub shared-world protocol including server-only authority. No TURN relay: some NAT/firewall pairs cannot connect. Rendering dependencies are embedded.';p.write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nbiome check --write src/main.js src/ui/interface.js --diagnostic-level=error --max-diagnostics=5\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Final polish and validation\n- Consolidated exact-artifact default verification passed235/235 before the final accessibility polish. Includes full stock solo, actual WebRTC UI, official5Hub scenarios, server-only host, honest timeout/results/end, real full stock372-event co-op route, WebGPU/WebGL2/WebKit and explicit unsupportedFirefox.\n- Focused file+touch suite then passed147/147. Final visual review found/verified fixes for modal opacity/native fade, credits navigation, native START overlap, mobile hidden-state CSS, saved glyph preference, Sound-off mix. All game/source files are implemented; no stubs.\n- Canonical report currently32 actual defects fixed (0critical), ledger docs/ISSUES.md explains each. The latest two are real co-op planning-time accessibility (negotiated invite2–30s, default8 stock) and mouse-motion attract exit. Keep tests/harness mistakes separate from defect count.\n- Multiplayer agent is adding invite planningSeconds validation/handshake/tests in src/net/network.js. API stable host({planningSeconds}), getters.rules/.planningSeconds; wait for agent final note before build. Root UI Settings.coopPlanning and invite disclosure implemented; online Dev now read-only.\n- Latest UI polish implemented but not yet rebuilt: focus after late custom content, phone floorheader width, gesture instructions moved into opening touch card (persistent hint hidden), mouse-motion attract exit, host planning setup row, aria labelMenu. Last canonical report32 needs complete final run.\n- Agent native visual-only review produced clean desktop modals/credits/phone menu at priorSHA4f47...; only persistent gesture hint overlapped, now hidden in source. No browser left by that agent. tools/visual-release.py --phone-only can verify final phone briefly. Source combat visuals already checked; no need unchanged fullvisual route again.\n- Root verification runs isolated on own ephemeral loopback ports, max2browser processes. tools/verify.mjs includes51core + now-growing network checks, package5, tools/browser-test.py, and default tools/network-release.py31extra. It checks evidence SHA matches artifact.\n- Next: finish agent planning API tests; add root UI negotiated12s probe + pointermotion attract test + actual Sound-off assertion already in browser-test.py; rebuild, run npmrunverify to green exact final SHA; phone-only visual proof. Then write docs/TESTING.md from actual counts and final report consistency/delivery links. Do not mutate production after final pass without new relevant check.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_167","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> src/ui/style.css <<'EOF'\n.touch-mode .place{max-width:75%}.touch-mode #touch-hint{display:none}\nEOF\ncat >> docs/ISSUES.md <<'EOF'\n\nThe long-menu focus fix in issue18 also rechecks focus after inserted developer/workshop content. The touch-HUD cleanup in issue28 now puts gesture instructions in the dismissible opening card and removes the overlapping persistent hint.\n\n31. Planning-window tuning could not affect a playable co-op setup, while standalone online developer controls appeared editable: noncritical configuration-access defect; validated host invitations now disclose/negotiate2–30-second planning (8 stock), custom durations mark the expedition modified, and all online developer panels are read-only.\n32. Meaningful mouse motion did not exit attract mode: noncritical input consistency defect; moving the mouse now exits and consumes the demo without starting a run.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('src/report.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text());r['testingFeedback'][0]='32 actual implementation issues were caught and fixed; the issue ledger separates them from test-harness mistakes.';r['sourceInformation']['online']='1–2 shared-world co-op: reliable ordered WebRTC DataChannel with manual offer/answer and disclosed 2–30-second planning (8 seconds stock); AI Hub shared-world protocol including server-only authority. No TURN relay: some NAT/firewall pairs cannot connect. Rendering dependencies are embedded.';p.write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nbiome check --write src/main.js src/ui/interface.js --diagnostic-level=error --max-diagnostics=5\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Final polish and validation\n- Consolidated exact-artifact default verification passed235/235 before the final accessibility polish. Includes full stock solo, actual WebRTC UI, official5Hub scenarios, server-only host, honest timeout/results/end, real full stock372-event co-op route, WebGPU/WebGL2/WebKit and explicit unsupportedFirefox.\n- Focused file+touch suite then passed147/147. Final visual review found/verified fixes for modal opacity/native fade, credits navigation, native START overlap, mobile hidden-state CSS, saved glyph preference, Sound-off mix. All game/source files are implemented; no stubs.\n- Canonical report currently32 actual defects fixed (0critical), ledger docs/ISSUES.md explains each. The latest two are real co-op planning-time accessibility (negotiated invite2–30s, default8 stock) and mouse-motion attract exit. Keep tests/harness mistakes separate from defect count.\n- Multiplayer agent is adding invite planningSeconds validation/handshake/tests in src/net/network.js. API stable host({planningSeconds}), getters.rules/.planningSeconds; wait for agent final note before build. Root UI Settings.coopPlanning and invite disclosure implemented; online Dev now read-only.\n- Latest UI polish implemented but not yet rebuilt: focus after late custom content, phone floorheader width, gesture instructions moved into opening touch card (persistent hint hidden), mouse-motion attract exit, host planning setup row, aria labelMenu. Last canonical report32 needs complete final run.\n- Agent native visual-only review produced clean desktop modals/credits/phone menu at priorSHA4f47...; only persistent gesture hint overlapped, now hidden in source. No browser left by that agent. tools/visual-release.py --phone-only can verify final phone briefly. Source combat visuals already checked; no need unchanged fullvisual route again.\n- Root verification runs isolated on own ephemeral loopback ports, max2browser processes. tools/verify.mjs includes51core + now-growing network checks, package5, tools/browser-test.py, and default tools/network-release.py31extra. It checks evidence SHA matches artifact.\n- Next: finish agent planning API tests; add root UI negotiated12s probe + pointermotion attract test + actual Sound-off assertion already in browser-test.py; rebuild, run npmrunverify to green exact final SHA; phone-only visual proof. Then write docs/TESTING.md from actual counts and final report consistency/delivery links. Do not mutate production after final pass without new relevant check.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"Skipped 49 suggested fixes.\nIf you wish to apply the suggested (unsafe) fixes, use the command biome check --write --unsafe\n\nChecked 2 files in 38ms. Fixed 2 files.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_168","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"tail -28 docs/network.md && rg -n 'planning|async host|encodeInvite' src/net/network.js | head -22 && rg -n 'Two adventurers|Host an expedition|separate browser peers' tools/browser-test.py | tail -8 && sed -n '588,622p' tools/browser-test.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_168","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"tail -28 docs/network.md && rg -n 'planning|async host|encodeInvite' src/net/network.js | head -22 && rg -n 'Two adventurers|Host an expedition|separate browser peers' tools/browser-test.py | tail -8 && sed -n '588,622p' tools/browser-test.py\"","aggregated_output":"\nThe expanded pure tests verify bounds and malformed values, legacy codes, wrong-answer rejection without SDP mutation, invalid Host options preserving an existing expedition, handshake mismatch rejection, the actual customized model deadline, stock-start equivalence, and canonical Hub initialization. A real two-context Chromium DataChannel probe additionally passes **9/9** checks: twelve-second offers/answers are disclosed and negotiated before play, mismatched answers preserve the pending offer, both peers receive modified twelve-second state, a real committed round gets the twelve-second deadline and resolves immediately when both plans arrive, and actual legacy offer/answer codes still start an unmodified eight-second run. This probe uses source modules; the root final-artifact suite covers the packaged UI and default full campaign.\n\n## AI Hub\n\nPinned client 1.4.0 (protocol 1) is copied unmodified into the delivery by the root builder. The adapter calls `AIHub.connect({mode:'shared-world',seats:[1,2]})`, installs lifecycle handlers, and defers `ready()` until rendering can begin. A `server:true` authority readies immediately and has no local adventurer. It needs neither renderer nor audio nor controller flow.\n\nThe Hub's synchronized clock is the only start gate: a start message alone cannot advance rules before `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Authority advances on a 25 ms timer independent of render frames or page visibility. Solo's `paused` flag is ignored online. Commands and all shared state travel through `AIHub.send` and message events; no WebRTC connection is created inside Hub sessions. Hub owns departures and host-loss policy.\n\nOnly authority calls finish, once. A team success requires a legitimately claimed treasure and an unmodified run. Timeout reports the actual incomplete state. End clears the simulation timer, outgoing messages, pending inputs, and resync buffers and calls the application end callback to stop audio. Current participant IDs form one tied team; result statistics report actual depth, treasure, boss defeat, and rounds.\n\n## Authority and traffic\n\nEvery packet includes protocol version, game ID, run ID, sender sequence, tick, floor, encounter ID, and round. The sender identity comes from the Hub's `from` or the established RTC peer role. Claimed player fields in actions never select the authoritative actor. Duplicates, unknown identities, old expeditions, wrong floors, and stale encounter/round commands are rejected. In particular, exploration movement queued before a combat trigger cannot silently become a tactical move.\n\nAuthority calls the production command handler in one serial JavaScript task. Clients receive explicit result acknowledgements and must await authority for loot, damage, doors, and progression. On each eight-Hz publication, the adapter sends a structural delta against its last published snapshot. Arrays replace atomically. Every three seconds it sends a versioned full JSON snapshot as bounded base64 chunks. Reliable ordering preserves the baseline before later deltas; a mismatch requests resynchronization. Snapshot graph size is capped at 320 KB; paths prohibit prototype modification. Packets remain below 15,200 UTF-8 bytes. A 65 ms send scheduler permits at most 16 packets/second without stalled-tab bursts, leaving headroom below Hub's 20/second limit. Client actions are coalesced into a bounded queue, sent at most eight per second; one heartbeat per second establishes return traffic during idle play.\n\n`diagnostics()` exposes mode, authority/server flags, run, clock state, connection/channel state, revision, queued traffic, rejected packets, largest actual packet, and maximum observed outbound messages/second. The release report and evidence are produced by the root's verification suite; implementation does not claim unrun browser or cross-network tests.\n\n## Verification completed during development\n\n`node tools/net-test.mjs` currently passes 22/22 pure protocol checks against the production model. The checks cover invite integrity/roles/run IDs, delta paths and schema, transport-derived identity, duplicate and old-run rejection, stale combat/floor commands, monotonic deadline synchronization on late receipt, production snapshot/delta agreement, departed gear recovery, and frozen authority after end.\n\n`/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python src/net/rtc-test.py` passes 14/14 real-DataChannel checks in two isolated Chromium contexts, exchanging actual gathered SDP codes through the production API. It covers both players' authoritative input, guest departure, cancel, fresh invitation retry, and host loss. It does not claim an inspected production invitation UI or internet NAT reachability.\n\n`/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python src/net/hub-test.py` runs the pinned official harness against a rendering-free source-module probe and passes five scenarios: two-player normal, two-player impaired (150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter, 5% loss), host-leave, impaired server-only authority with two players, and one-player Hub. Reports assert both `dataset.complete` and `__hubCheck.pass`. Largest observed packet: 10,156 bytes; maximum observed outbound messages in a second: 14. These are transport probes; the root integration suite must separately verify the final bundled game, game-specific interactions, and its full rendering/UI lifecycle.\n\nNetwork state never overwrites solo progression. The adapter's `allowSoloSave` is true only for a run started through `startSolo`; RTC/Hub set it false, and it remains false when a host continues alone after their guest leaves. The application's autosave must honor this flag.\n66:\tif (value === undefined) return { planningSeconds: STOCK_PLANNING_SECONDS };\n69:\t\tObject.keys(value).some((key) => key !== \"planningSeconds\") ||\n70:\t\t!Number.isInteger(value.planningSeconds) ||\n71:\t\tvalue.planningSeconds < 2 ||\n72:\t\tvalue.planningSeconds > 30\n76:\treturn { planningSeconds: value.planningSeconds };\n79:export function encodeInvite(description, run, rules = undefined) {\n321:\tget planningSeconds() {\n322:\t\treturn this.rules.planningSeconds;\n475:\tasync host(options = {}) {\n477:\t\t\tthrow new Error(\"Host options must describe a planning window.\");\n479:\t\t\toptions.planningSeconds === undefined\n481:\t\t\t\t: { planningSeconds: options.planningSeconds },\n503:\t\tconst code = encodeInvite(this.pc.localDescription, this._run, this.rules);\n505:\t\t\t`Offer ready · ${this.planningSeconds}-second planning window${this.planningSeconds === STOCK_PLANNING_SECONDS ? \" · stock rules\" : \" · modified expedition\"}. Send it to your partner, then paste th [... omitted end of long line]\n524:\t\t\t`Host chose a ${this.planningSeconds}-second planning window${this.planningSeconds === STOCK_PLANNING_SECONDS ? \" · stock rules\" : \" · modified expedition\"}. Gathering your answer…`,\n544:\t\tconst code = encodeInvite(this.pc.localDescription, this._run, this.rules);\n546:\t\t\t`Answer ready · ${this.planningSeconds}-second planning window accepted. Send it to the host and leave this page open.`,\n560:\t\tif (invite.rules.planningSeconds !== this.planningSeconds)\n562:\t\t\t\t`The answer accepts a different planning window. This offer requires ${this.planningSeconds} seconds. Ask your partner to use your current offer.`,\n714:\t\tif (this.planningSeconds !== STOCK_PLANNING_SECONDS) {\n715:\t\t\tthis.model.setTuning({ planningSeconds: this.planningSeconds });\n140:        'document.activeElement.textContent===\"Two adventurers\"',\n147:        page.evaluate(\"document.activeElement.textContent\") == \"Two adventurers\",\n642:            page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Two adventurers\", exact=True).click()\n651:        a.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Host an expedition\", exact=True).click()\n678:            \"separate browser peers own separate adventurers\",\n            prefix,\n        )\n        page.locator(\"[data-source=guard]\").tap()\n        page.locator(\"#context-action\").tap()\n        page.wait_for_function('__app.ui.selected!==\"guard\"', timeout=5000, polling=50)\n        check(\n            device + \" touch guard returns to attack selector\",\n            page.evaluate(\"__app.state.stats.rounds\") > 0,\n        )\n        context.close()\n    browser.close()\n\n\nclass QuietHandler(http.server.SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def log_message(self, format: str, *args: object) -> None:\n        pass\n\n\ndef server_start():\n    server = http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer(\n        (\"127.0.0.1\", 0), functools.partial(QuietHandler, directory=str(WORK))\n    )\n    thread = threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\n    thread.start()\n    return server, thread\n\n\ndef rtc_checks(pw):\n    server, thread = server_start()\n    browser = launch(pw.chromium, headless=True, args=FLAGS)\n    url = (\n        f\"http://127.0.0.1:{server.server_port}/\"\n        + urllib.parse.quote(CONFIG[\"html\"])\n        + \"?backend=webgl\"\n    )\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_169","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('tools/browser-test.py');s=p.read_text()\nanchor='''        a.get_by_role(\\\"button\\\", name=\\\"Host an expedition\\\", exact=True).click()\n'''\naddition='''        a.get_by_role(\\\"slider\\\",name=\\\"Host planning window\\\",exact=True).fill(\\\"12\\\")\n        a.get_by_role(\\\"slider\\\",name=\\\"Host planning window\\\",exact=True).dispatch_event(\\\"input\\\")\n''';assert anchor in s;s=s.replace(anchor,addition+anchor)\nanchor='''        answer = b.locator(\\\"#invite-output\\\").input_value()\n'''\naddition='''        check(\\\"guest sees negotiated planning duration before returning answer\\\",b.evaluate(\\\"__app.net.planningSeconds\\\") == 12 and \\\"12\\\" in b.locator('.connection-status').inner_text())\n''';assert anchor in s;s=s.replace(anchor,anchor+addition)\nanchor='''        # Follow commands through actual pads/UI and authority, never optimistic client awards.\n'''\naddition='''        check(\\\"custom planning window is authoritative and marked modified\\\",a.evaluate(\\\"__app.state.tuning.planningSeconds===12&&__app.state.modified\\\") and b.evaluate(\\\"__app.state.tuning.planningSeconds===12&&__app.state.modified\\\"))\n''';assert anchor in s;s=s.replace(anchor,addition+anchor)\nanchor='''    check(\n        \\\"attract never overwrites solo save\\\",\n'''\naddition='''    page.evaluate(\\\"__DANGER.setIdle(10001);__app.update(0)\\\")\n    page.mouse.move(21,21)\n    page.wait_for_function(\\\"__app.stage==='title'&&\"'!__app.attract\",timeout=5000,polling=50)\n    check(\"meaningful mouse motion exits and consumes attract demo\",page.evaluate(\"__app.ui.shell.screen==='\"'title'\\\"))\n''';assert anchor in s;s=s.replace(anchor,addition+anchor)\nanchor='''        page.get_by_role(\\\"button\\\", name=\\\"Enter the vault\\\", exact=True).tap()\n'''\naddition='''        check(device+\\\" gets dismissible gesture instructions\\\", \\\"drag the left half\\\" in page.locator('.screen-briefing').inner_text())\n''';assert anchor in s;s=s.replace(anchor,addition+anchor)\nanchor='''    check(\\\"developer mode reachable through pause\\\", page.evaluate(\\\"__app.ui.shell.screen\\\") == \\\"dev\\\")\n'''\n# The formatted source wraps this check; positive focus assertion is inserted before locating the first slider.\nanchor='''    slider = page.get_by_role(\\\"slider\\\", name=\\\"Player damage ×\\\", exact=True)\n'''\naddition='''    check(\\\"developer initial focus is on a visible tuning control\\\",page.evaluate(\\\"(()=>{const e=document.activeElement,r=e.getBoundingClientRect();return e.type==='range'&&r.top>=0&&r.bottom<=innerHeight})()\\\"))\n''';assert anchor in s;s=s.replace(anchor,addition+anchor)\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nruff check --fix tools/browser-test.py && ruff format tools/browser-test.py && ty check tools/browser-test.py --python /home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\nnode --check src/main.js && node --check src/ui/interface.js && node --check src/net/network.js\nnpm run build && npm run verify\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
