{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_185","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,hashlib\nroot=Path('.')\nconfig=json.loads((root/'build-config.json').read_text())\nartifact=(root.parent/config['html']).resolve()\nsha=hashlib.sha256(artifact.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\nb=json.loads((root/'evidence/release-file-touch-rtc-hub-fallbacks.json').read_text())\nn=json.loads((root/'evidence/network-release-rtc-hub.json').read_text())\nassert b['failed']==0 and n['failed']==0\nassert b['artifactSha256']==sha==n['evidence']['artifactSha256']\nassert json.loads((root.parent/'exit-interview.json').read_text())==json.loads((root/'src/report.json').read_text())\nrt=n['evidence']['rtc']\ndiagnostics=rt['diagnostics']+[d for x in b['evidence']['hubReports'] for d in x.get('diagnostics',[])]\nmax_bytes=max(d['traffic']['maxBytes'] for d in diagnostics)\nmax_rate=max(d['traffic']['maxPerSecond'] for d in diagnostics)\nreport=f'''# Release verification\n\nFinal command: \"'`npm run verify` → **249/249 checks passed; 0 failures.**\n\nDelivered artifact: `{config['\"'html']}\"'`  \nSize: {artifact.stat().st_size:,} bytes.  \nSHA-256: `{sha}`\n\n| Group | Checks | Evidence |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Deterministic rules, content, saves and full routes | 51 | tools/rules-test.mjs |\n| Transport authority, timing, codecs and negotiated windows | 22 | tools/net-test.mjs |\n| Package, client placement and canonical report | 5 | tools/verify.mjs |\n| Delivered HTML browser/input/audio/RTC UI/official Hub/renderers | {b['\"'total']} | evidence/release-file-touch-rtc-hub-fallbacks.json |\n| Delivered HTML complete real co-op and Hub edge cases | {n['total']} | evidence/network-release-rtc-hub.json |\n\nBoth browser evidence reports identify this exact final SHA. The verification runner rejects stale evidence or a different artifact hash.\n\n## Full normal-rules expeditions\n\nSolo:175 accepted production commands,92 steps,38 resolved rounds,all3 floors,8 defeated enemies,8 rests,one secret,one gate,both damage channels,permanent War/Spirit training,trap disarm,upgrades,all3 guardian seals and an explicit treasure claim. Ends38War/26Spirit. Invulnerability and modified balance remain false. The script separately asserts boss-defeated and treasure-not-yet-claimed before the final interaction.\n\nReal cooperative route:372 interleaved commands (370 accepted and2 deliberate full-pack comparison refusals),198 steps,66 rounds,8 enemies,2 personal gate crossings,all3 guardian phases,and deliberate treasure claim. Every command travels through production handlers and the real reliable ordered WebRTC channel; both peers' semantic gameplay state is compared after every acknowledged event. The stock run remains unmodified. Automated replay elapsed {rt['elapsedSeconds']:.2f}s; this is a machine replay, not a human playtime estimate. Cosmetic RAF is stopped during the dense command replay while the independent authority/network timer remains live; rendering/UI boot is verified before, and ending UI after. No health,ammo,position,enemy or balance mutation occurs in either full route.\n\nScenario tests use explicitly controlled setup states for contested loot,handoff,revival,disconnect and timeout cases. Those setup fixtures are separate from stock-route completion evidence; they are not presented as no-cheat campaigns.\n\n## Session and transport coverage\n\nThe pinned official harness passed normal2-player,150ms latency/50ms jitter/5%loss,host-leave,server-only authority with2 players,and1-player scenarios. Every run waited for \"'`document.body.dataset.complete === \"true\"` and required `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`.\n\nAdditional exact-HTML checks cover actual nonhost departure,active boss-phase timeout,downed-state timeout,one honest authority result,current-participant standings,zero outgoing traffic or state advance after end,and a stock full Hub victory before its real time cap. A server-only copy has no Game,renderer,audio context or local avatar. Settings stay live online. Controller loss does not freeze the shared world.\n\nActual Host/Join UI codes establish two isolated browser contexts. Malformed invites remain recoverable. A12-second setup selection is disclosed before the guest returns an answer,negotiated through the connection,and applied to both authoritative/shared views with a modified flag. Stock and Hub remain8 seconds. Pure transport tests additionally reject invalid durations,mismatched answers,stale/duplicate/foreign commands and unsafe resync paths.\n\nLargest measured release packet across the final full RTC/official Hub evidence: {max_bytes:,} bytes; largest observed outbound rate: {max_rate}/second. All packets use reliable ordered delivery and remain within Hub'\"'s16KB/20-message limits. These are protocol checks,not graphics benchmarks.\n\n## Rendering,input,persistence and audio\n\nThe final file boots under file:// with embedded engine,three module graph and embedded Rapier WASM. Request inspection observed only the game document (and its reload); no neighboring source,CDN,JSON,image,audio or separate WASM requests. WebGPU state and WebGL2 fallback both pass. WebKit's available WebGL2 path passes. This Firefox installation has no WebGL and receives a clear unsupported-renderer/retry screen.\n\nInput coverage includes a standard-mapping pad stub (D-pad navigation,PS/Xbox prompts,L3 map,action selection,disconnect/reconnect),keyboard movement and menus,rebindings,actual mouse look,phone/tablet touch,multitouch,context actions and guard recovery. Native long-menu focus,credits scrolling,developer sliders/reset and content validation are checked. Attract starts at the10-second boundary,exits on consumed input/mouse movement,and leaves solo saves unchanged. A real page reload preserves glyph preferences and the versioned solo checkpoint; corrupt and blocked storage remain playable.\n\nMusic defaults0.10. OfflineAudioContext renders the same original instrument/voice functions:44,100 finite samples,36,400 nonzero,peak0.0560,RMS0.00526,no clipping,and muted output exactly zero. The native Sound-off preference also mutes the custom synth. No human listening was available.\n\n## Visual inspection and limits\n\nInspected TV title,first room,pack,map,pause/developer,credits,ordinary enemy silhouettes,Spirit chamber,boss and stock victory. The final phone review uses390×844 and confirms visible menus,one menu button,visible initial developer-slider focus,and no observed HUD/context/counter overlap. Evidence files record their own SHA. The final post-review edits clarify credits and exact numerical gate/trap previews; core art,layout,inputs and transport are unchanged from the inspected build. The final249-check run was performed after those edits.\n\nNo physical controller,touch hardware,real iOS device,TV,second human,human audio listening or cross-network NAT test was available. Emulated device and same-machine peer success do not establish universal hardware/internet reachability. No TURN relay is supplied. The declared10-minute Hub duration is the intended human pacing,not a measured human run.\n\nDefect counts:32 actual implementation issues,all fixed;0 classified critical/game-breaking. See docs/ISSUES.md. Harness mistakes (including string-search false positives,synthetic pointer capture and object-order comparisons) are recorded separately and not counted as game defects.\n'''\n(root/'docs/TESTING.md').write_text(report)\n(root/'build/release-summary.json').write_text(json.dumps({'artifact':str(artifact),'sha256':sha,'bytes':artifact.stat().st_size,'checks':249,'failures':0,'rules':51,'protocol':22,'packaging':5,'browser':b['total'],'cooperativeRelease':n['total'],'maxPacketBytes':max_bytes,'maxMessagesPerSecond':max_rate},indent=2))\nprogress=(root.parent/'PROGRESS.md')\nprogress.write_text(progress.read_text()+f'''\\\\n\\\\n## COMPLETE\\\\n- Game built and verified; no required work remains.\\\\n- Root deliverable: {config['html']} ({artifact.stat().st_size:,}bytes).\\\\n- Root machine-readable report: exit-interview.json; exact canonical copy of src/report.json, parsed and checked.\\\\n- Final SHA256: {sha}.\\\\n- Final \"'`npm run verify`:249/249 passed,0failures (51rules,22protocol,5package,140browser,31full-co-op/Hubedge). Both release reports match final artifactSHA.'\"\\\\n- Complete stock solo175actions/38rounds and real stock co-op372events/66rounds; bothchannels,allfloors/enemies,secret/gate/trap/training/recovery,3bossphases,and explicittreasureclaim proven.\\\\n- Official finalHTML Hub scenarios5/5 pass; server-only no renderer/audio; stock Hub victory; actual timeout/downed/leave/end cases.\\\\n- Real UI planningtime12s negotiation works;8s default/Hub;custommarkedmodified.\\\\n- File/WebGL2,WebGPU,WebKit and unsupportedFirefox paths; controller/KBM/rebinding,phone/tablet/multitouch,preferences/save/retry/attract/dev/content/audio all checked.\\\\n- Latest phonevisualreview clean at recordedSHA8d8198...; final follow-up changed only license wording and exact numerical gate/trap preview text. Final249tests rerun afterallchanges. See docs/TESTING.md and evidence reports.\\\\n-32actualimplementationdefects fixed,0critical; docs/ISSUES.md. Required source info/4testing/6engine/4prompt answers complete in-game and exit-interview.json. Usage exactly added on import.\\\\n- No owned test server/browser intentionally left running. Do not rerun unchanged checks; final reply should link HTML/report/progress and include all4 required feedback sections with source fields/order from canonical report.\\\\n''')\nprint(json.dumps({'sha256':sha,'checks':249,'failures':0,'maxPacketBytes':max_bytes,'maxMessagesPerSecond':max_rate,'reportMatches':True}))\nPY\npython3 -m json.tool ../exit-interview.json >/dev/null\nls -lh ../*.html ../exit-interview.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
